# Git and authorship

**Do not commit or push.** The operator commits. Do not `git commit`,
`git push`, `--amend`, or skip hooks unless the user explicitly asks in that
turn.

When you do commit:

- Do not add `--trailer` or a `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
  line. The operator is the only author.
- Do not update git config, force-push, or skip hooks unless asked.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, vault files, tokens).
